! mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap -- "PARAMETER POOL", printed page 116.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.123, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID
! DD000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 116".
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The card-serial column
! restarts at DD000001 (line 1) and runs to DD000033 (line 38);
! printed p.112 was punching DB0000xx.  THIRTY-EIGHT LINES, COUNTED
! NOT ESTIMATED: the printed LINE column runs 1..38 with no gap, the
! serial column was rendered whole in two crops, and the form is
! blank below line 38.  Thirty-three cards for thirty-eight lines --
! six serials repeat (DD000007, 15, 17, 21, 26 each cover two
! lines), which is this listing's usual one-card/two-listed-lines
! habit.
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  Lines 1-3 are the banner "PARAMETER
! POOL".  The page is MCP's pool of scalar parameters and save
! areas, in four parts:
!
!   lines  7-11  five scalar parameters, named by their own comment
!                column and not interpreted further here: S BNDRS
!                plus an unnamed second half word, together one full
!                word, commented "-MCP BOUNDS" and carrying the
!                values 33 and 32; S MAXUB, "-MAXIMUM UPPER BOUNDS
!                FOR PP"; S PS IOI, an XW, "-I/O INTERRUPT
!                PRESERVATION WORD"; and S IT BAS, "-BASE ADDRESS OF
!                INTERRUPT TABLE", whose VF operand is S IT.  What
!                the two bounds values are counted IN is not stated
!                on this page and is not guessed at here; the volume
!                OCR shows something addressing bits within 215224
!                ("215224.06 10  LX,$3,YSFBCR").
!   lines 13-31  FOUR IDENTICAL 29-WORD SAVE REGIONS, one per level,
!                each a "DRZ(BU,64), 29" followed by a half word for
!                the saved instruction counter and a NOP that pads
!                the region out to a full word:
!                   S T LR   215230.00..215264  then S T IC  215265.00
!                   S LR PP  215266.00..215322  then S IC PP 215323.00
!                   S LR BU  215324.00..215360  then S IC BU 215361.00
!                   S LR MCP 215362.00..215416  then S IC MCP 215417.00
!                The first and third regions carry two SYN views of
!                their first word -- S UPPER / S LOWER on S T LR,
!                S PP UB / S PP LB on S LR BU -- the upper and lower
!                PP boundaries, at +0 and +.32 of the same word.
!                The MCP region alone has a word planted INSIDE it:
!                lines 27-28 SLC back to S LR MCP+9.0 and punch an
!                INDMK there (see ASSEMBLER LIMITATIONS below).
!   lines 33-36  S QUE, the 128-slot 19-bit interrupt queue
!                (-INTERRUPT QUEUE), S CUM Q its current pointer,
!                YMISCO the maskable interrupt counter, and S READS
!                the read-source XW.
!   lines 37-38  S COMM, "B,MCOMD" -- the emergency entry to the
!                commentator -- and S COMIC beside it.
!
! THE ASTERISK IN THE LOCATION COLUMN.  Lines 5, 13, 18, 21, 26, 29
! and 33 print a "*" after the location (every DRZ and two of the
! three SLCs; line 27's SLC does not).  It is recorded on the !CHECK
! notes where there is a row to carry it and is not interpreted here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE SITS -- BOTH JOINS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS NOT SET BY AN ADDRESSED CARD ON THIS PAGE. <<<
! Line 5 is "SLC,$" -- the counter set to itself -- and the page
! prints 215224.00 beside it.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000."
! is the last addressed SLC before here.  The arriving counter is
! confirmed from the volume's own OCR: docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt
! for PDF p.122 (printed p.115) ends at its line 16, "215223.4C
! 216531.1C CO  B,YMSF" -- a half word at 215223.40, which ends
! exactly at 215224.00.  THE BACKWARD JOIN IS CONTIGUOUS.
!
! This deck writes a hard "SLC, (8)215224." ahead of the printed
! "SLC,$" so that it assembles standalone.  THAT ROW IS NOT ON THE
! PAGE and is flagged at the statement; it is the row to reconsider
! when pp.113-115 land, exactly as printed p.112's deck says of its
! own.
!
! >>> AND "SLC,$" IS INERT IN strap_asm, WHICH IS WORTH KNOWING
! BEFORE pp.113-115 LAND. <<<  Measured, not assumed, twice:
! deleting the "SLC, $" row and re-running the page verifier gives
! the identical 41 PASS / 1 FAIL, and "SLC,(8)1000.40 / SLC,$ / X
! VF,0" puts X at 1000.40 -- so "$" does NOT round the counter up to
! a word boundary.  The hard SLC above is therefore what actually
! places this page, and the printed row cannot cover for it being
! wrong.  (Line 6's CNOP is what would do any rounding, and on this
! page it emits nothing, so the counter really does arrive on
! 215224.00 already aligned.)
!
! THE PAGE LEAVES THE COUNTER AT 215471.00 -- line 38's VF half word
! sits at 215470.40 -- and nothing here is checked against p.117.
!
! pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that printed p.2 opened
! and printed p.98 line 37 closed with "UNTAIL,(2)", so a name here
! may legitimately repeat a name from pp.2-98 at a different address.
! That is tail scope, not a collision.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NAMES: THIRTEEN OF THE TWENTY-TWO ARE SETTLED BY DOCUMENT, NOT INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This drum opens round glyphs, so O/C was decided by grep wherever
! a second witness exists.  docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt and
! .../MCP_Mar63_250-445.txt are full-volume OCRs of this same
! listing -- garbled, so a CROSS-CHECK and never a source, but they
! name a symbol beside its octal address, and the octal survives OCR
! far better than the letters do.  Grepping THIS PAGE'S ADDRESSES
! turned up a reference for thirteen of its twenty-two symbols:
!
!   215225  "SV,$11,SMAXUB" and "KV,..,SMAXUB CHECK FOR BOUNDS"
!   215226  p.112 lines 12-16 "BZB1,S PS IOI+.9 ,K STORE"  (and the
!           MCP System Analysis Guide's interrupt table prints
!           "SPSIOI (receptor)" in type, which is what settles the
!           O; printed p.112's deck already carries that spelling
!           and this deck matches it)
!   215230  "TI,13,$UB,S TLR" and "T,15,STLR,S LR PP"
!           (this file quoted it as "T1" until 2026-10-31; T1 is
!            not a Transmit mnemonic -- opcodes.TRANSMIT_CODES is
!            T/TI/TB/TBI plus the SWAPs -- and printed p.122's
!            glyph has an I's top and bottom bars.  Comment only;
!            no check consumed it, which is why it survived.)
!   215265  "SIC,STIC", dozens of times on printed pp.110-111
!   215266  "T,15,STLR,S LR PP"
!   215324  "KV,$1,SLRBU"
!   215362  "T,15,S TLR,S LR MCP"
!   215420  "LVI,8,S QUE"
!   215466  "LV,8,S CUM Q" and "LC,$1,YMISCO" / "SC+$1,YMISCO"
!   215467  "SX,$13,SREADS"
!   215470  "B,S COMM" and "SIC,S COM IC"
!
! >>> AND THREE OF THEM ARE SETTLED IN TYPE, BY A DIFFERENT
! DOCUMENT. <<<  docs/ocr/C22-6728*_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt is
! typeset, not drum-printed:
!   "YMISCO - Maskable interrupt counter, reset to ..."  -- which is
!       this page's own line-35 comment, "-MASKABLE INTERRUPT
!       COUNTER", word for word.  The last glyph is an O.
!   "SREADS - the read source control is an XW whose ..."  -- this
!       page's line 36 IS that XW, and its comment is "-READ SOURCE
!       WORD."
!   "MCOMD when being used by a disabled MCP program", and "BD,
!       MCOMD" -- line 37's branch target.
! and the same guide's "the saved IC is stored in STIC", with 37 and
! 38 hits for STIC and ZERO for STIO across its two revisions.
!
! >>> THAT LAST ONE CLOSES A QUESTION THE NEIGHBOURING DECKS LEFT
! OPEN. <<<  printed p.112's deck records (its line 183) that the
! OCR read this page's 215265.00 row as "S T IO" and that at 1200 dpi
! the glyph is open on the right.  This page is the DEFINING card and
! it reads "S T IC"; it is also the only member of its family that
! would not fit the pattern otherwise -- S T LR/S T IC, S LR PP/S IC
! PP, S LR BU/S IC BU, S LR MCP/S IC MCP, four regions each with its
! own saved IC.  pp.110 and 111 both already carry "STIC SYN,(8)
! 215265.0"; this deck's spelling agrees with theirs and with the
! manual.
!
! >>> S COMIC IS CORROBORATED FROM THE OTHER VOLUME. <<<
! docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_250-445.txt PDF p.53 is the COMMENTATOR page,
! whose "COMMENTATOR DISABLED ENTRY POINT" is labelled MCOMD -- line
! 37's target -- and three rows below it prints "215470.41 80 ...
! $XC,SCOMIC  -ADVANCE SCOMIC TO EXIT SETTING".  That names S COMIC
! at this page's 215470.40 from a page nobody has transcribed.
!
! >>> TWO NAMES REST ON INK ALONE. <<<  S BNDRS (line 7) and S IT
! BAS (line 11) occur nowhere else in either volume's OCR or in any
! manual.  Both were re-read at 1800 dpi: in "BNDRS" the B has the
! flat stemmed left side of a B and not the round left of an 8, and
! the D has the straight vertical left stem that separates it from
! C/O; "BAS" prints the same B.  The comments agree with both
! readings -- line 8's "-MCP BOUNDS" for BNDRS, and line 11's "-BASE
! ADDRESS OF INTERRUPT TABLE" with the operand S IT for IT BAS -- but
! neither name has a second witness and both are flagged here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO ASSEMBLER GAPS THIS PAGE FOUND -- BOTH NOW FIXED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 28 is "INDMK,$IF".  When this page was transcribed strap_asm
! refused it twice over; both refusals were real gaps, both are
! fixed, and the statement is live with its !CHECK passing.
!
! (1) AN INDICATOR MNEMONIC NAMES A BIT, NOT AN ADDRESS.  eval_expr
!     maps "$IF" to the bit ADDRESS 11*64+21 = 725 (word 11, the
!     indicator word), and 725 is not a bit of a word.  C28-6129
!     printed p.19's own example is "INDMK, $ZM, $EXE, $IF", so the
!     dollar form is the documented way to write an indicator mask --
!     which is what INDMK is FOR.  INDMK now reads INDICATOR_BITS for
!     a $-name.  THIS PAGE IS THE WITNESS: the printed
!     "000000.04 00  000000.00 00" is bits 18-23 = 0o04, i.e. bit 21
!     alone, and 21 is indicator IF.
!
! (2) A DRZ'S ZERO FILL IS A RESERVATION, NOT CONTENT.  Line 26
!     reserves 29 words; line 27's "SLC,S LR MCP+9.0" goes back
!     INSIDE that region and line 28 punches a word there.  IBM's
!     assembler accepted it -- the page prints the result -- and
!     strap_asm refused with "two statements deposited overlapping
!     bits in word 72443".  C22-6531 printed p.35 says DRZ is
!     "exactly the same fashion as DR with one exception: the fields
!     reserved are all set to zero", and printed p.44 adds that "DRZ
!     yields THE SAME SIZE OF BINARY DECK AS DR" -- a DR punches no
!     data for its reservation, so neither does a DRZ.  The zeros are
!     a DEFAULT and content written over them wins.  Image.deposit
!     now clears a DRZ fill rather than refusing it, and a DRZ over
!     ALREADY-WRITTEN bits is still an error.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE ORACLE DOES NOT CHECK ON THIS PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Eleven of the 38 rows carry no checkable binary and are recorded
! in the listing block below without a !CHECK:
!
!   lines 1-4    comment cards (the banner); no location, no binary.
!   lines 5,27,29  SLC rows: a location and no binary.
!   lines 6,32   CNOP rows that emitted NOTHING because the counter
!                was already on a word boundary -- neither prints a
!                location.  (Line 12's CNOP DID emit, at 215227.40,
!                and IS checked.)
!   lines 13,18,21,26,33  the DRZ rows.  Their BINARY OUTPUT column
!                prints the RESERVATION LENGTH, not storage --
!                "000035.00" is 0o35 = 29 words and "000046.00" is
!                0o46 = 38 words (128 slots x 19 bits = 2432 bits).
!                listing_oracle has no renderer for that, so the
!                lengths are transcribed and recorded, not verified.
!                They ARE verified indirectly: each region's length
!                is exactly what puts the NEXT named row on its
!                printed location, and all 22 !SYM addresses match.
!   lines 14,15,22,23  the SYN rows.  As on printed p.103, the data
!                descriptions they print in the binary column
!                ("+00000000   BU,100,10" -- mode BU, length 0o100 =
!                64, byte size 0o10 = 8) are not checked; the !SYM
!                lines check their ADDRESSES and nothing else.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- EXTERNALS -----------------------------------------------------
! S IT is NOT back-derived: printed p.103's deck already carries
! "SIT SYN,(8)215023.0" on printed p.110's label, so line 11's
! printed 215023.00+ is an independent cross-check of this page.
SIT     SYN, (8)215023.0             ! line 11 operand; p.110 label
! MCOMD IS back-derived from line 37 alone and this !CHECK is to that
! extent a tautology, as p.103's ZFINIS was.  What is NOT a tautology
! is the OP BYTE: B compiles 00 here with no help from the symbol.
! Note the .10 -- printed p.112 established that B prints its target
! plus 0o10 in the bit field ("B,W LODE" on WLODE at 216333.0 prints
! 216333.10), so the SYMBOL is 233150.00 and the row prints 233150.10.
MCOMD   SYN, (8)233150.0             ! line 37 "B,MCOMD"

! ---- THE PAGE ------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)215224.              ! NOT A CARD ON THIS PAGE -- the
                                     ! arriving counter, written hard so
                                     ! the deck assembles alone.  p.115's
                                     ! last row ends at 215224.00.
!   line  1  - **********************************************
!   line  2  -                PARAMETER POOL
!   line  3  - **********************************************
!   line  4  -
        SLC, $                       ! line  5
        CNOP                         ! line  6  (emits nothing)
SBNDRS  VF, 33.0                     ! line  7
        VF, 32.0                     ! line  8  -MCP BOUNDS
SMAXUB  VF, 0.0                      ! line  9  -MAXIMUM UPPER BOUNDS FOR PP
SPSIOI  XW, 0                        ! line 10  -I/O INTERRUPT PRESERVATION WORD
SITBAS  VF, SIT                      ! line 11  -BASE ADDRESS OF INTERRUPT TABLE
        CNOP                         ! line 12  (emits a NOP at 215227.40)
STLR    DRZ(BU,64), 29               ! line 13
SUPPER  SYN, STLR                    ! line 14  -PP UPPER BOUNDRY
SLOWER  SYN, STLR+0.32               ! line 15
STIC    VF, 0                        ! line 16
        NOP                          ! line 17
SLRPP   DRZ(BU,64), 29               ! line 18
SICPP   VF, 0                        ! line 19
        NOP                          ! line 20
SLRBU   DRZ(BU,64), 29               ! line 21
SPPUB   SYN, SLRBU                   ! line 22
SPPLB   SYN, SLRBU+.32               ! line 23  -SAVED UPPER AND LOWER BOUNDARIES
SICBU   VF, 0                        ! line 24
        NOP                          ! line 25
SLRMCP  DRZ(BU,64), 29               ! line 26
        SLC, SLRMCP+9.0              ! line 27
        INDMK, $IF                   ! line 28 -- SEE "ASSEMBLER
                                     ! LIMITATIONS" ABOVE.  The page
                                     ! punches one word of bit 21 at
                                     ! 215373.00, inside the region line
                                     ! 26 reserved.  strap_asm cannot
                                     ! express it: "$IF" resolves to bit
                                     ! 725, and even "INDMK,21" is refused
                                     ! because the word overlaps the DRZ
                                     ! fill.  The row's !CHECK is kept and
                                     ! FAILS, on purpose.
        SLC, SLRMCP+29.0             ! line 29
SICMCP  VF, 0                        ! line 30
        NOP                          ! line 31
        CNOP                         ! line 32  (emits nothing)
SQUE    DRZ(BU,19),(128)             ! line 33  -INTERRUPT QUEUE
SCUMQ   VF, SQUE                     ! line 34
YMISCO  CF, 50                       ! line 35  -MASKABLE INTERRUPT COUNTER
SREADS  XW, 0                        ! line 36  -READ SOURCE WORD.
SCOMM   B, MCOMD                     ! line 37  -EMERGENCY ENTRY TO COMMMENTATOR
SCOMIC  VF, 0                        ! line 38
        END

! ---- THE PRINTED LISTING, AS READ ----------------------------------
!  line  loc          binary output                      name     statement
!    1                                                   -  *********************
!    2                                                   -      PARAMETER POOL
!    3                                                   -  *********************
!    4                                                   -
!    5   215224.00 *                                              SLC,$
!    6                                                            CNOP
!    7   215224.00    000041.00+                         S BNDRS  VF,33.0
!    8   215224.40    000040.00+                                  VF,32.0
!    9   215225.00    000000.00+                         S MAXUB  VF,0.0
!   10   215226.00    000000.00+ 000 000000 000000       S PS IOI XW,0
!   11   215227.00    215023.00+                         S IT BAS VF,S IT
!   12   215227.40    000000.30 00                                CNOP
!   13   215230.00 *  000035.00                          S T LR   DRZ(BU,64), 29
!   14   215230.00+   +00000000      BU,100,10           S UPPER  SYN,S TLR
!   15   215230.40+   +00000000      BU,100,10           S LOWER  SYN,S TLR+0.32
!   16   215265.00    000000.00+                         S T IC   VF, 0
!   17   215265.40    000000.30 00                                NOP
!   18   215266.00 *  000035.00                          S LR PP  DRZ(BU,64), 29
!   19   215323.00    000000.00+                         S IC PP  VF, 0
!   20   215323.40    000000.30 00                                NOP
!   21   215324.00 *  000035.00                          S LR BU  DRZ(BU,64), 29
!   22   215324.00+   +00000000      BU,100,10           S PP UB  SYN,S LR BU
!   23   215324.40+   +00000000      BU,100,10           S PP LB  SYN,S LR BU+.32
!   24   215361.00    000000.00+                         S IC BU  VF, 0
!   25   215361.40    000000.30 00                                NOP
!   26   215362.00 *  000035.00                          S LR MCP DRZ(BU,64), 29
!   27   215373.00                                                SLC,SLRMCP+9.0
!   28   215373.00    000000.04 00  000000.00 00                  INDMK,$IF
!   29   215417.00 *                                              SLC,SLRMCP+29.0
!   30   215417.00    000000.00+                         S IC MCP VF, 0
!   31   215417.40    000000.30 00                                NOP
!   32                                                            CNOP
!   33   215420.00 *  000046.00                          S QUE    DRZ(BU,19),(128)
!   34   215466.00    215420.00+                         S CUM Q  VF,S QUE
!   35   215466.40    000062                             YMISCO   CF,50
!   36   215467.00    000000.00+ 000 000000 000000       SREADS   XW,0
!   37   215470.00    233150.10 00                       S COMM   B,MCOMD
!   38   215470.40    000000.00+                         S COMIC  VF,0

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 116 ------------------
!SYM   SBNDRS   215224.00
!SYM   SMAXUB   215225.00
!SYM   SPSIOI   215226.00
!SYM   SITBAS   215227.00
!SYM   STLR     215230.00
!SYM   SUPPER   215230.00
!SYM   SLOWER   215230.40
!SYM   STIC     215265.00
!SYM   SLRPP    215266.00
!SYM   SICPP    215323.00
!SYM   SLRBU    215324.00
!SYM   SPPUB    215324.00
!SYM   SPPLB    215324.40
!SYM   SICBU    215361.00
!SYM   SLRMCP   215362.00
!SYM   SICMCP   215417.00
!SYM   SQUE     215420.00
!SYM   SCUMQ    215466.00
!SYM   YMISCO   215466.40
!SYM   SREADS   215467.00
!SYM   SCOMM    215470.00
!SYM   SCOMIC   215470.40

!CHECK 215224.00 | 000041.00+ | line 7 S BNDRS VF,33.0
!CHECK 215224.40 | 000040.00+ | line 8 (unnamed) VF,32.0 -MCP BOUNDS
!CHECK 215225.00 | 000000.00+ | line 9 S MAXUB VF,0.0
!CHECK 215226.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 10 S PS IOI XW,0
!CHECK 215227.00 | 215023.00+ | line 11 S IT BAS VF,S IT -- S IT is p.110's label, not back-derived here
!CHECK 215227.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 12 CNOP (this one emits)
!CHECK 215265.00 | 000000.00+ | line 16 S T IC VF,0 -- this is STIC, referenced by pp.110-111
!CHECK 215265.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 17 NOP
!CHECK 215323.00 | 000000.00+ | line 19 S IC PP VF,0
!CHECK 215323.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 20 NOP
!CHECK 215361.00 | 000000.00+ | line 24 S IC BU VF,0
!CHECK 215361.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 25 NOP
!CHECK 215373.00 | 000000.04 00 000000.00 00 | line 28 INDMK,$IF -- EXPECTED TO FAIL: statement commented out, see ASSEMBLER LIMITATIONS (bit 21, planted inside line 26's DRZ region)
!CHECK 215417.00 | 000000.00+ | line 30 S IC MCP VF,0 -- 215417.00 itself prints no asterisk; line 29's SLC prints the same location WITH one
!CHECK 215417.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 31 NOP
!CHECK 215466.00 | 215420.00+ | line 34 S CUM Q VF,S QUE
!CHECK 215466.40 | 000062 | line 35 YMISCO CF,50 -- 0o62 = 50, an 18-bit count field
!CHECK 215467.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 36 SREADS XW,0
!CHECK 215470.00 | 233150.10 00 | line 37 S COMM B,MCOMD -- MCOMD back-derived; the 00 op byte is not
!CHECK 215470.40 | 000000.00+ | line 38 S COMIC VF,0
